Package: wallloop
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: amd64
Section: web
Priority: optional
Maintainer: ericbyz <ericbyz@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: systemd
Description: NAS dynamic wallpaper service (Wallpaper-Engine class, original)
 WallLoop is an original, self-hosted dynamic wallpaper service for TOS.
 It stores a wallpaper library (video/image) on the NAS, plays it fullscreen
 in any browser at http://<NAS>:18240/play (TV/tablet/phone, read-only public
 surface), rotates the playlist on an interval or by day/night time slots,
 and synthesizes demo wallpapers locally with the factory ffmpeg (no bundled
 or CDN media assets). A Chinese-first original admin panel lives behind the
 TOS desktop floating window (admin surface on 127.0.0.1 only, nginx-proxied
 at /wallloop/). Client API: GET /api/v1/now.
 Source and reproducible build: https://github.com/ericbyz/wallloop
